    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0259" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/6–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-02T19:00:00-04:00">June 2, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Since Moscow has already released to the press a version of the Dimitrov
                    case the Department is releasing a statement by the Acting Secretary<anchor
                        n="80" xml:id="d231-f1"/> which is being sent to you separately.<anchor
                        n="81" xml:id="d231-f2"/> We of course appreciate the cogency of your
                    recommendations against publicity (urtel 290 June 2) except for this revelation
                    at Moscow of which you were doubtless unaware. Let us have your further
                    recommendations in the light of your continuing conversations.</p>
                <p>As regards the note to the ACC proposed in your 291 just received it seems to us
                    that in view of the foregoing developments it may be better to delay any reply
                    whatever to the ACC pending Regent Ganev’s further efforts and the reaction to
                    the public statements on the case.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow, Caserta and London.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d231-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
